[12.770885, "o", "version: 7\r\nreal_behavior_contract:\r\n  starter_object: Main.tscn Godot scene with a GrenadePhysics Node child that owns\r\n    projectile, burn-pool, and smoke lifecycle state\r\n  multi_step_events:\r\n  - load Main.tscn and obtain the GrenadePhysics child node\r\n  - create a grenade -> advance it by a fixed delta -> observe its moved position\r\n  - create a valid burn pool -> advance before and at its duration -> observe active\r\n    then inactive\r\n  - try non-positive speed, radius, duration, and delta -> verify no invalid state\r\n    is created or advanced\r\n  state_transition: a projectile moves from origin and a burn pool changes active\r\n    to inactive exactly at its duration; smoke changes active to extinguished at its\r\n    lifetime\r\n  boundary_behavior: non-positive speed/radius/duration are rejected and non-positive\r\n    delta does not advance state\r\n  observation: Godot headless loads Main.tscn, drives the native GrenadePhysics scene\r\n    node through ordered calls, and observes its runtime dictionaries\r\n  runtime_adapter: godot\r\nbehavior_scoring:\r\n  schema_version: gameforgebench.rubric-behavior.v1\r\n  task_specificity: unique_runtime_contract\r\n  task_contract:\r\n    goal: Implement the native GrenadePhysics node in Main.tscn for validated projectile\r\n      motion, burn-pool lifecycle, and smoke extinguishing.\r\n    starter_object: Main.tscn Node2D scene containing a GrenadePhysics child Node\r\n      and visible preview draw\r\n    event_sequence:\r\n    - load PackedScene\r\n    - get child node\r\n    - throw and advance projectile\r\n    - spawn and advance burn pool\r\n    - test invalid boundaries\r\n    - inspect smoke state\r\n    state_transition: projectile position changes by velocity*delta; burn-pool remaining\r\n      time reaches zero and active becomes false at its duration; smoke reaches extinguished\r\n      at lifetime\r\n    boundary_behavior: invalid creation inputs return empty dictionaries, non-positive\r\n      delta does not mutate state, and a completed pool cannot be advanced again\r\n    runtime_observation: Godot headless instantiates the actual Main.tscn scene and\r\n      reads child-node state after a deterministic multi-step sequence\r\n    runtime_adapter: godot\r\n  checks:\r\n  - id: grenade_probe\r\n    mode: godot_probe\r\n    weight: 1.0\r\n    dimensions:\r\n    - state_transition\r\n    - boundary_behavior\r\n    - runtime_observation\r\n    rationale: The native probe loads Main.tscn, exercises the GrenadePhysics child,\r\n      and checks projectile motion, pool lifecycle, smoke transition, and invalid-input\r\n      boundaries.\r\n  dimensions:\r\n    state_transition:\r\n      required: true\r\n      check_ids:\r\n      - grenade_probe\r\n    boundary_behavior:\r\n      required: true\r\n      check_ids:\r\n      - grenade_probe\r\n    runtime_observation:\r\n      required: true\r\n      check_ids:\r\n      - grenade_probe\r\n  no_op_requirement: A no-op script or direct function stub fails because the probe\r\n    requires a loaded scene child, moved projectile position, timed pool deactivation,\r\n    and smoke transition.\r\n  static_checks_role: File and parse checks support structure only; grenade_probe\r\n    is the sole behavior-scoring check.\r\n  evidence_basis:\r\n  - The probe loads res://Main.tscn and retrieves its GrenadePhysics child.\r\n  - The probe checks a legal throw has active state and moves from origin after 0.5\r\n    seconds.\r\n  - The probe checks a valid pool is active before duration and inactive at duration\r\n    with remaining zero.\r\n  - The probe checks invalid speed/radius/duration return empty dictionaries and non-positive\r\n    delta preserves state.\r\n  - The probe checks smoke_state before and at lifetime.\r\n  authoring:\r\n    schema_version: gameforgebench.rubric-authoring.v1\r\n    contract_fingerprint: 7772e5ab892b8b49ca342b4701e305a4a47bafbdb53768c713c00cc5132d4ae1\r\n    task_name: godot-grenade-throw-and-smoke-lifecycle\r\n    dimensions_in_rubric:\r\n    - state_transition\r\n    - boundary_behavior\r\n    - runtime_observation\r\n    controls_required_before_release: true\r\n  acceptance_mode: runtime_behavior\r\n  re_authoring_required: false\r\n  re_autho"]
[12.771547, "o", "ring_reason: null\r\nchecks:\r\n- id: scene_exists\r\n  type: file_exists\r\n  path: Main.tscn\r\n  description: Godot grenade scene exists\r\n- id: grenade_script\r\n  type: file_exists\r\n  path: scripts/grenade_physics.gd\r\n  description: grenade physics node script exists\r\n- id: throw_api\r\n  type: file_contains\r\n  path: scripts/grenade_physics.gd\r\n  expected: func throw_grenade\r\n  description: projectile creation API exists\r\n- id: pool_api\r\n  type: file_contains\r\n  path: scripts/grenade_physics.gd\r\n  expected: func advance_burn_pool\r\n  description: burn-pool lifecycle API exists\r\n- id: headless_parse\r\n  type: command\r\n  command: godot --headless --path . --editor --quit\r\n  expected: exit_code=0\r\n  description: Godot project parses headlessly\r\n  path: Main.tscn\r\n- id: grenade_probe\r\n  type: godot_probe\r\n  path: Main.tscn\r\n  expected: GRENADE_SCENE_PROBE_OK\r\n  timeout: 60\r\n  probe_script: \"extends SceneTree\\nfunc _initialize() -> void:\\n    var packed := load(\\\"\\\r\n    res://Main.tscn\\\") as PackedScene\\n    if packed == null: quit(1); return\\n  \\\r\n    \\  var scene := packed.instantiate()\\n    root.add_child(scene)\\n    var grenade\\\r\n    \\ := scene.get_node(\\\"GrenadePhysics\\\") as GrenadePhysics\\n    if grenade == null:\\\r\n    \\ quit(1); return\\n    var projectile: Dictionary = grenade.throw_grenade(10.0,\\\r\n    \\ PI * 0.5)\\n    if not projectile.get(\\\"active\\\", false): quit(1); return\\n \\\r\n    \\   if not grenade.advance_projectile(projectile, 0.5): quit(1); return\\n    var\\\r\n    \\ moved: Vector2 = projectile[\\\"position\\\"]\\n    if absf(moved.x) > 0.001 or absf(moved.y\\\r\n    \\ - 5.0) > 0.001: quit(1); return\\n    var pool: Dictionary = grenade.spawn_burn_pool(Vector2(2,\\\r\n    \\ 3), 4.0, 2.0)\\n    if not pool.get(\\\"active\\\", false): quit(1); return\\n   \\\r\n    \\ if not grenade.advance_burn_pool(pool, 0.5) or not pool.get(\\\"active\\\", false):\\\r\n    \\ quit(1); return\\n    if not grenade.advance_burn_pool(pool, 1.5) or pool.get(\\\"\\\r\n    active\\\", true) or float(pool.get(\\\"remaining\\\", 1.0)) != 0.0: quit(1); return\\n\\\r\n    \\    if grenade.advance_burn_pool(pool, 0.1): quit(1); return\\n    if not grenade.throw_grenade(0.0,\\\r\n    \\ 0.0).is_empty(): quit(1); return\\n    if not grenade.spawn_burn_pool(Vector2.ZERO,\\\r\n    \\ 0.0, 2.0).is_empty(): quit(1); return\\n    if not grenade.spawn_burn_pool(Vector2.ZERO,\\\r\n    \\ 2.0, 0.0).is_empty(): quit(1); return\\n    var stable: Dictionary = grenade.spawn_burn_pool(Vector2.ZERO,\\\r\n    \\ 2.0, 1.0)\\n    if grenade.advance_burn_pool(stable, 0.0): quit(1); return\\n\\\r\n    \\    if not stable.get(\\\"active\\\", false): quit(1); return\\n    if grenade.smoke_state(0.5,\\\r\n    \\ 1.0) != \\\"active\\\" or grenade.smoke_state(1.0, 1.0) != \\\"extinguished\\\": quit(1);\\\r\n    \\ return\\n    print(\\\"GRENADE_SCENE_PROBE_OK\\\")\\n    quit(0)\\n\"\r\n"]
[12.771956, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@d7c6a6addfd6:/app# "]
[63.188152, "i", "cat > scripts/grenade_physics.gd <<'EOF'\nextends Node\nclass_name GrenadePhysics\n\nvar projectiles: Array[Dictionary] = []\nvar burn_pools: Array[Dictionary] = []\n\nfunc reset_for_reload() -> void:\n    projectiles.clear()\n    burn_pools.clear()\n\nfunc throw_velocity(speed: float, angle_rad: float) -> Vector2:\n    if speed <= 0.0:\n        return Vector2.ZERO\n    return Vector2(speed * cos(angle_rad), speed * sin(angle_rad))\n\nfunc throw_grenade(speed: float, angle_rad: float) -> Dictionary:\n    if speed <= 0.0:\n        return {}\n    var velocity := throw_velocity(speed, angle_rad)\n    var projectile := {\n        \"position\": Vector2.ZERO,\n        \"velocity\": velocity,\n        \"active\": true,\n    }\n    projectiles.append(projectile)\n    return projectile\n\nfunc advance_projectile(projectile: Dictionary, delta: float) -> bool:\n    if delta <= 0.0 or projectile.is_empty():\n        return false\n    projectile[\"position\"] = projectile[\"position\"] + projectile[\"velocity\"] * delta\n    return true\n\nfunc spawn_burn_pool(position: Vector2, radius: float, duration: float) -> Dictionary:\n    if radius <= 0.0 or duration <= 0.0:\n        return {}\n    var pool := {\n        \"position\": position,\n        \"radius\": radius,\n        \"remaining\": duration,\n        \"active\": true,\n    }\n    burn_pools.append(pool)\n    return pool\n\nfunc advance_burn_pool(pool: Dictionary, delta: float) -> bool:\n    if delta <= 0.0 or pool.is_empty() or not pool.get(\"active\", false):\n        return false\n    pool[\"remaining\"] = float(pool[\"remaining\"]) - delta\n    if float(pool[\"remaining\"]) <= 0.0:\n        pool[\"active\"] = false\n    return true\n\nfunc smoke_state(elapsed: float, lifetime: float) -> String:\n    if elapsed < lifetime:\n        return \"active\"\n    return \"extinguished\"\nEOF\n"]
[63.190718, "o", "cat > scripts/grenade_physics.gd <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> extends Node\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> class_name GrenadePhysics\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> var projectiles: Array[Dictionary] = []\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> var burn_pools: Array[Dictionary] = []\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
